  "term": "Down syndrome",
  "definition": "Down syndrome is a chromosome disorder caused by an extra chromosome 21 or its equivalent. It is associated with a characteristic pattern of physical features, moderate to severe intellectual disability, and increased risk of certain medical problems including heart and gastrointestinal abnormalities, leukemia, and early-onset Alzheimer disease.",
